  "attributes": {
    "long_name": "raw sensor counts",
    "units": "1",
    "coordinates": "exposures",
    "ancillary_variables": "hemisphere_disk_mask",
    "black_level": 64,
    "white_level": 1023,
    "comment": "Analog-to-digital counts, stored exactly as the 10-bit sensor reported them, cropped to a fixed bounding box around the imaged disk. Stored in the squished (de-interleaved) sub_y/sub_x layout -- each Bayer band as its own coherent half-resolution image, one per `band` -- because that compresses far better under JPEG-XL than the interleaved mosaic. Pixel validity is derived, not stored: a pixel is underexposed where raw <= black_level (64), overexposed where raw >= white_level (1023), and valid in between (65..1022). Counts a few below the black level occur as read noise around the black-level pedestal and count as underexposed. Whether a pixel lies within the imaged hemisphere is answered by hemisphere_disk_mask; whether it sees open sky is a further, world-frame question answered in the next-level product.",
    "zarr_chunks": {
